    "body": "Hi ajnart,\n\nThanks for the suggestion, but I don't think that is the right solution.\n\nWhen any user starts configuring Homarr, even if they have read the documentation in full, it is an experiment. And even if you get the board ordering perfect first time, there is no saying when you will want to add another board out of position (or split a board so that you don't have to page scroll).  The current system is far too rigid and inflexible, adding a keybind only adds another workflow step which in itself would not match with the current workflow, it does not solve the underlaying issue.\n\nIn may case I have a 8 node Proxmox cluster running at home, so I could never get away with a 1 or 2 pages dashboard, once you get above that level, the board ordering really matter as you want the most used boards at the top of the list, and that ordering can change over time.",
